WEBVTT

00:11:29.876 --> 00:11:31.756
difficult question to answer.

00:11:31.756 --> 00:11:34.516
Because it’s quite exciting.

00:11:34.556 --> 00:11:37.236
Afterwards, you’re like,
“Ooh, that was really exciting.”

00:11:37.236 --> 00:11:38.996
But at the time, it’s quite humbling.

00:11:38.996 --> 00:11:41.236
Because I think you’re kind of
aware of the fact

00:11:41.276 --> 00:11:44.476
you’re seven miles underwater
and one ton per square centimeter

00:11:44.476 --> 00:11:46.716
and all that kind of,
you do feel quite remote.

00:11:46.716 --> 00:11:49.196
But I just think it looks
kind of majestic.

00:11:49.196 --> 00:11:52.076
I think it's certainly
the exact polar opposite

00:11:52.116 --> 00:11:54.396
of what you're told it should be like.

00:11:54.396 --> 00:11:57.916
It’s not scary, it’s peaceful,
and it’s nice, and there’s beauty there.

00:11:57.956 --> 00:12:02.196
And I think we need to challenge
the narratives that we are given